WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.240
The Foundation once tried to kill SCP-682,
the Hard to Destroy Reptile, with SCP-272,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.600
an old iron nail.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.080
This anomalous nail can kill its victims in
a number of ways: The nail bind’s a victim’s

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.160
shadow to the ground, indirectly binding the
victim itself as well by doing so.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.720
If the shadow is displaced due to changes
in light source, the victim is flung and contorted

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.960
in the same direction the shadow has moved.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.640
If the victim tries to destroy the nail, they
will surely die.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.200
After the Foundation intentionally made the
lights in 682’s chamber strobe on and off

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.120
from various directions, causing the reptile
to be mutilated by being hurled around the

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:35.440
room.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.480
Its body began producing an extremely powerful
light source, eliminating its own shadow and

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.680
keeping it safe.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.920
The light was so bright that when D-Classes
entered the chamber to remove the nail - despite

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.600
wearing eye protection - they were afflicted
with permanent retinal damage.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.840
And of course - in the end - SCP-682 was just
fine.

